sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs).
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1-22 (one cfgmgmt systemd apply, its check as the end check, no shipped scripts; rule 21: only this command's branches).
  %% Rule 23: 2026-11-03 required-only main path.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: process:start
  %% kind: process.start
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: process:start 417
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:start 417`
  %%> - syntax: `process:start <process> [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Process ID from `process:list`
  %%> Optional:
  %%> - `--idempotency-key` reuses a task start; `--json` returns JSON; neither adds a step
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 417: provisioning · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Node that runs Process 417
  %%> - Process 417 exists and is not being removed
  %%> - a production Process's release is checked against the recorded releases, not on the Node
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent: unit or container name, runtime, on-demand flag, Vite plan
  %%> - Process 417 marked provisioning; its desired state does not change yet
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-control
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.start
  %%> - the Process unit or container name, runtime and on-demand flag
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> Checked by the input schema:
  %%> - no step reads or re-checks the intent
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt Vite dev Process
    SW->>N: Publish the dev route<br/>native Vite workflow
  end
  alt systemd
    SW->>N: Start the Process<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.apply
    SW->>N: Check the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.check
  else Docker
    SW->>N: Start the container<br/>ssh exec · docker start
    SW->>N: Check the container<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_container
  else Instance container
    SW->>N: Act in the container<br/>Ansible · tags process
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the Process is an `orbit` unit in its Instance container; the child run `operation-process-container` changes it through `incus exec` on the Node and checks its state
    %%> - systemd starts use nonblocking jobs; readiness reads have 5-second bounds, with 10 retries at 1-second intervals
    %%> - a stopped container fails the change; its next deployment starts it
  end
  opt Vite dev Process
    SW->>N: Check the listener<br/>ssh exec · ss
    SW->>N: Mark it awake<br/>cfgmgmt/file
  end
  SW->>N: Verify the state<br/>native assert
  %%> The pinned checks report compliance; native assert fails the run on drift.
  alt Process active
    N-->>SW: active
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Process is active
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the end check's output; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Process: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 417 desired state becomes running; its status becomes active
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds with the observed state
  else start or verify fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, the unit is missing, or the state does not match
    %%> How:
    %%> - the failing step ends the run with its own exit code; there is no report step
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its exit code, mapped to `error_code`
    Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 417 is marked failed with the error code; its desired state does not change
    %%> - task #5130 fails
    %%> - there is no rollback and nothing to clean up; run the same command again after fixing the cause
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
